module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.DenseSubsite.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.GlobalSectionsClosed.InverseImage
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.EtaleUniversalHomeomorphism
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Topological invariance of the small étale site: the site-theoretic reduction

Stacks Project Tag 04DZ (EGA IV, Theorem 18.1.2) says that base change along a universal
homeomorphism `f : X ⟶ Y` is an equivalence between the schemes étale over `Y` and the schemes
étale over `X`. The sheaf-theoretic consequences drawn from it, such as
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.smallEtaleInverseImage_isEquivalence_of_isDenseSubsite` and
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.etaleCohomologyRestrictionMap_bijective_of_isDenseSubsite`, are packaged
through a single hypothesis: that base change is a *dense subsite inclusion* of the small étale
site of `Y` into that of `X`.

This file reduces that hypothesis to its two genuinely geometric halves. A dense subsite
inclusion consists of four conditions, and two of them are proved here outright, for an
arbitrary surjective morphism of schemes: base change is faithful, and a sieve on the small
étale site of `Y` is covering exactly when its image is covering. What remains is fullness of
base change (Tag 0BTY) and cover-density (the essential surjectivity half of Tag 04DZ); both are
carried as hypotheses, and `isCoverDense_smallEtaleBaseChange_iff` says in elementary terms what
cover-density asks for.

## Main results

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff`: a sieve on an object of the small
  étale site is covering exactly when the images of its arrows cover the underlying space.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.isPullback_smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left`: base change along `f`
  carries a morphism of the small étale site of `Y` to a pullback of it.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.smallEtaleBaseChange_faithful`: base change along a surjective
  morphism is faithful on small étale sites.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.functorPushforward_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff`: for `f`
  surjective, a sieve is covering on the small étale site of `Y` exactly when its image under
  base change is covering on that of `X`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.isCoverDense_smallEtaleBaseChange_iff`: base change is
  cover-dense exactly when every point of every scheme étale over `X` is in the image of a
  morphism to it from a base change of a scheme étale over `Y`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.isDenseSubsite_of_full_of_isCoverDense`: base change along a
  surjective morphism is a dense subsite inclusion as soon as it is full and cover-dense.

## Implementation notes

The small étale site is Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Etale` with the topology
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.smallEtaleTopology`, and base change is
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.smallEtaleBaseChange`, the restriction of
`CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.Over.pullback` to étale objects. On underlying morphisms it is
given by the same `CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback.lift` as the slice pullback, so
`forget_map_smallEtaleBaseChange_map` identifies the two and lets the hom-level statements
proved for `CategoryTheory.Over.pullback` be transported.

Mathlib's covering criterion `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff` is
stated for a sieve presented by a family of arrows. Since a sieve is the sieve generated by the
family of *all* of its arrows, indexing that family by
`Σ V, {g : V ⟶ W // S.arrows g}` turns the criterion into the pointwise statement
`mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff`, which is what both directions of
`functorPushforward_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff` are checked against.

The reflecting direction uses only that `pullback.fst V.hom f`, the base change of `f`, is
surjective. The preserving direction uses that base change of a morphism of the small étale site
of `Y` is literally a pullback of it, `isPullback_smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left`, so that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_preimage_of_isPullback` lifts points. Neither direction needs
`f` to be injective or closed, so both hold for an arbitrary surjection.

## References

* [EGA IV, Theorem 18.1.2]
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04DZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04DZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BTY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BTY)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

universe u

namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology

section Covering

variable {Z : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A sieve on an object `W` of the small étale site of a scheme is covering exactly when every
point of the underlying scheme of `W` lies in the image of one of its arrows.

This is Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff` for an
arbitrary sieve rather than for a sieve presented by a family of arrows. -/
theorem mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff {W : Z.Etale} (S : Sieve W) :
    S ∈ smallEtaleTopology Z W ↔
      ∀ w : W.left, ∃ (V : Z.Etale) (g : V ⟶ W), S.arrows g ∧ w ∈ Set.range g.left := by
  classical
  let ι : Type (u + 1) := Σ V : Z.Etale, {g : V ⟶ W // S.arrows g}
  let obj : ι → Z.Etale := fun i => i.1
  let arr : ∀ i : ι, obj i ⟶ W := fun i => i.2.1
  have hS : Sieve.ofArrows obj arr = S :=
    le_antisymm (by rw [Sieve.ofArrows, Sieve.generate_le_iff]; rintro V g ⟨i⟩; exact i.2.2)
      fun V g hg => Sieve.ofArrows_mk obj arr ⟨V, ⟨g, hg⟩⟩
  have key := Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff arr
  rw [hS] at key
  rw [key]
  constructor
  · intro h w
    have hw : w ∈ ⋃ i, Set.range (arr i).left := by rw [h]; exact Set.mem_univ w
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp hw
    exact ⟨i.1, i.2.1, i.2.2, hi⟩
  · intro h
    ext w
    simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, Set.mem_univ, iff_true]
    obtain ⟨V, g, hg, hw⟩ := h w
    exact ⟨⟨V, ⟨g, hg⟩⟩, hw⟩

end Covering

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Base change along `f` sends a morphism of the small étale site of `Y` to the canonical
`CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback.lift`, exactly as the slice pullback does. -/
theorem smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left (f : X ⟶ Y) {V V' : Y.Etale} (g : V' ⟶ V) :
    ((smallEtaleBaseChange f).map g).left =
      pullback.lift (pullback.fst V'.hom f ≫ g.left) (pullback.snd V'.hom f)
        (by rw [Category.assoc, MorphismProperty.Over.w g, pullback.condition]) :=
  rfl

/-- Base change along `f` commutes with the forgetful functor to the slice category: on
morphisms it is the slice pullback. -/
theorem forget_map_smallEtaleBaseChange_map (f : X ⟶ Y) {V W : Y.Etale} (h : V ⟶ W) :
    (Scheme.Etale.forget X).map ((smallEtaleBaseChange f).map h) =
      (CategoryTheory.Over.pullback f).map ((Scheme.Etale.forget Y).map h) :=
  rfl

/-- Base changing a composable pair: if `ab = a ≫ b`, then the comparison map
`A ×_Y X ⟶ B ×_Y X` exhibits `A ×_Y X` as the fibre product of `A` and `B ×_Y X` over `B`. -/
theorem isPullback_pullbackFst_pullbackLift {A B : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (b : B ⟶ Y)
    (a : A ⟶ B) (ab : A ⟶ Y) (hab : a ≫ b = ab) :
    IsPullback (pullback.fst ab f)
      (pullback.lift (pullback.fst ab f ≫ a) (pullback.snd ab f)
        (by rw [Category.assoc, hab, pullback.condition]))
      a (pullback.fst b f) := by
  subst hab
  refine IsPullback.of_bot ?_ (pullback.lift_fst _ _ _).symm (IsPullback.of_hasPullback b f)
  rw [pullback.lift_snd]
  exact IsPullback.of_hasPullback (a ≫ b) f

/-- The base change along `f` of a morphism `g` of the small étale site of `Y` is a pullback
of `g`: the square with sides the two first projections, `g` and the base change of `g`, is
cartesian. -/
theorem isPullback_smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left (f : X ⟶ Y) {V V' : Y.Etale} (g : V' ⟶ V) :
    IsPullback (pullback.fst V'.hom f) ((smallEtaleBaseChange f).map g).left
      g.left (pullback.fst V.hom f) := by
  rw [smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left]
  exact isPullback_pullbackFst_pullbackLift f V.hom g.left V'.hom (MorphismProperty.Over.w g)

/-- The commuting square of `isPullback_smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left`, read on points. -/
theorem smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left_apply (f : X ⟶ Y) {V V' : Y.Etale} (g : V' ⟶ V)
    (p : (pullback V'.hom f : Scheme.{u})) :
    g.left ((pullback.fst V'.hom f) p) =
      (pullback.fst V.hom f) (((smallEtaleBaseChange f).map g).left p) :=
  congrArg (fun k : (pullback V'.hom f : Scheme.{u}) ⟶ V.left => k p)
    (isPullback_smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left f g).w

/-- **Base change along a surjection is faithful on small étale sites.** A morphism of schemes
étale over `Y` is determined by its base change along any surjection onto `Y`.

This is the faithfulness half of Stacks Project, Tag 0BTY, and it holds for any surjective `f`:
it is `Stacks.Etale.injective_baseChange_hom_of_surjective` read on the small étale site. -/
@[ega "IV 2.2.16" "Both S-schemes étale", sga "3 X 2.0" "faithfulness"]
instance smallEtaleBaseChange_faithful (f : X ⟶ Y) [Surjective f] :
    (smallEtaleBaseChange f).Faithful where
  map_injective {V W} h₁ h₂ e := by
    have hW : Etale ((Scheme.Etale.forget Y).obj W).hom := W.prop
    refine (Scheme.Etale.forget Y).map_injective ?_
    refine Stacks.Etale.injective_baseChange_hom_of_surjective f
      ((Scheme.Etale.forget Y).obj W) ((Scheme.Etale.forget Y).obj V) ?_
    change (CategoryTheory.Over.pullback f).map ((Scheme.Etale.forget Y).map h₁) =
      (CategoryTheory.Over.pullback f).map ((Scheme.Etale.forget Y).map h₂)
    rw [← forget_map_smallEtaleBaseChange_map, ← forget_map_smallEtaleBaseChange_map, e]

/-- Base change along a universal homeomorphism is faithful on small étale sites. -/
theorem smallEtaleBaseChange_faithful_of_universalHomeomorphism (f : X ⟶ Y)
    [UniversalHomeomorphism f] : (smallEtaleBaseChange f).Faithful :=
  have := Stacks.Etale.surjective_of_universalHomeomorphism f
  smallEtaleBaseChange_faithful f

/-- **Base change along a surjection neither creates nor destroys coverings.** For `f`
surjective, a sieve on an object of the small étale site of `Y` is covering exactly when its
image under base change is covering on the small étale site of `X`.

This is the condition `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsDenseSubsite.functorPushforward_mem_iff`, the
last of the four requirements for base change to be a dense subsite inclusion. Both directions
use only surjectivity of `f`. -/
theorem functorPushforward_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff (f : X ⟶ Y) [Surjective f] {V : Y.Etale}
    (S : Sieve V) :
    S.functorPushforward (smallEtaleBaseChange f) ∈
        smallEtaleTopology X ((smallEtaleBaseChange f).obj V) ↔
      S ∈ smallEtaleTopology Y V := by
  rw [mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff, mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff]
  constructor
  · intro h v
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (show Surjective (pullback.fst V.hom f) from inferInstance).surj v
    obtain ⟨U, m, ⟨V', g, k, hg, hm⟩, w, hw⟩ := h z
    refine ⟨V', g, hg, (pullback.fst V'.hom f) (k.left w), ?_⟩
    have hz' : ((smallEtaleBaseChange f).map g).left (k.left w) = z := by
      rw [← hw, hm]; rfl
    exact (smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left_apply f g _).trans ((congrArg _ hz').trans hz)
  · intro h z
    obtain ⟨V', g, hg, v', hv'⟩ := h ((pullback.fst V.hom f) z)
    obtain ⟨w, _, hw⟩ := Scheme.exists_preimage_of_isPullback
      (isPullback_smallEtaleBaseChange_map_left f g) v' z hv'
    exact ⟨(smallEtaleBaseChange f).obj V',
      (smallEtaleBaseChange f).map g,
      Presieve.image_mem_functorPushforward _ S.arrows hg, w, hw⟩

/-- **What cover-density of base change asks for.** Base change along `f` is cover-dense for the
small étale topology on `X` exactly when every point of every scheme étale over `X` lies in the
image of a morphism to it from the base change of a scheme étale over `Y`.

Equivalently: the base changes `X ×_Y V` are jointly surjective onto every `U` étale over `X`.
For a universal homeomorphism this is the essential surjectivity half of Stacks Project,
Tag 04DZ, localised on the small étale site. -/
theorem isCoverDense_smallEtaleBaseChange_iff (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    (smallEtaleBaseChange f).IsCoverDense (smallEtaleTopology X) ↔
      ∀ (U : X.Etale) (u : U.left), ∃ (V : Y.Etale)
        (m : (smallEtaleBaseChange f).obj V ⟶ U), u ∈ Set.range m.left := by
  constructor
  · intro hd U u
    have := hd
    obtain ⟨U', h, ⟨c⟩, w, hw⟩ := (mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff _).1
      (Functor.is_cover_of_isCoverDense (smallEtaleBaseChange f)
        (smallEtaleTopology X) U) u
    have hfac : c.lift.left ≫ c.map.left = h.left :=
      congrArg (fun t : U' ⟶ U => t.left) c.fac
    refine ⟨c.obj, c.map, c.lift.left w, ?_⟩
    rwa [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hfac]
  · intro hd
    refine ⟨fun U => (mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff _).2 fun u => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨V, m, w, hw⟩ := hd U u
    exact ⟨_, m, Presieve.in_coverByImage _ m, w, hw⟩

/-- **The reduction of the dense subsite hypothesis.** For `f` surjective, base change exhibits
the small étale site of `Y` as a dense subsite of that of `X` as soon as it is full and
cover-dense.

Faithfulness and the covering criterion come from surjectivity alone, by
`smallEtaleBaseChange_faithful` and `functorPushforward_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff`; local
fullness and local faithfulness then follow from fullness and faithfulness. So for a universal
homeomorphism the dense subsite hypothesis of
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.smallEtaleInverseImage_isEquivalence_of_isDenseSubsite` reduces to
exactly two statements: fullness of base change (Stacks Project, Tag 0BTY) and cover-density
(Stacks Project, Tag 04DZ, essential surjectivity), the latter spelled out in
`isCoverDense_smallEtaleBaseChange_iff`. -/
theorem isDenseSubsite_of_full_of_isCoverDense (f : X ⟶ Y) [Surjective f]
    [(smallEtaleBaseChange f).Full]
    [(smallEtaleBaseChange f).IsCoverDense (smallEtaleTopology X)] :
    (smallEtaleBaseChange f).IsDenseSubsite
      (smallEtaleTopology Y) (smallEtaleTopology X) where
  functorPushforward_mem_iff := functorPushforward_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff f _

/-- The reduction of the dense subsite hypothesis for a universal homeomorphism: base change is a
dense subsite inclusion as soon as it is full and cover-dense. -/
theorem isDenseSubsite_of_universalHomeomorphism_of_full_of_isCoverDense (f : X ⟶ Y)
    [UniversalHomeomorphism f] [(smallEtaleBaseChange f).Full]
    [(smallEtaleBaseChange f).IsCoverDense (smallEtaleTopology X)] :
    (smallEtaleBaseChange f).IsDenseSubsite
      (smallEtaleTopology Y) (smallEtaleTopology X) :=
  have := Stacks.Etale.surjective_of_universalHomeomorphism f
  isDenseSubsite_of_full_of_isCoverDense f

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology

end
